{"seconds": 34.4, "exit": 0, "final": "These knight moves don't accomplish much. **bxc3+** is clearly the best\u2014it wins a rook by force.\n\n**Best move:** bxc3+\n\n**Main line:** bxc3+ Kb3 (or Ka3/Kc1/Kb1/Ka1) cxd2, winning White's rook.\n\n**Motif:** deflection and fork\n\n**Coaching note:** \nWhen an enemy piece is attacked but defended, look for a forcing move that attacks the defender. Here, bxc3+ checks the king and threatens the rook on d2. After the king moves, cxd2 captures the undefended rook\u2014you've deflected the king away from its job defending. Always examine checks that also threaten other pieces!\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"bxc3+\", \"line\": [\"bxc3+\", \"Kb3\", \"cxd2\", \"Rxd2\", \"fxe6\"], \"motifs\": [\"deflection\", \"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r1r3k1/4npp1/3RN2p/p3p3/1p2P3/2P2P1P/PKPR1BP1/8 b - - 0 22"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r1r3k1/4npp1/3RN2p/p3p3/1p2P3/2P2P1P/PKPR1BP1/8 b - - 0 22"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r1r3k1/4npp1/3RN2p/p3p3/1p2P3/2P2P1P/PKPR1BP1/8 b - - 0 22", "square": "d6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r1r3k1/4npp1/3RN2p/p3p3/1p2P3/2P2P1P/PKPR1BP1/8 b - - 0 22", "square": "d2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r1r3k1/4npp1/3RN2p/p3p3/1p2P3/2P2P1P/PKPR1BP1/8 b - - 0 22", "square": "c8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r1r3k1/4npp1/3RN2p/p3p3/1p2P3/2P2P1P/PKPR1BP1/8 b - - 0 22", "square": "a8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "r1r3k1/4npp1/3RN2p/p3p3/1p2P3/2P2P1P/PKPR1BP1/8 b - - 0 22", "square": "e6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r1r3k1/4npp1/3RN2p/p3p3/1p2P3/2P2P1P/PKPR1BP1/8 b - - 0 22"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1r3k1/4npp1/3RN2p/p3p3/1p2P3/2P2P1P/PKPR1BP1/8 b - - 0 22", "move": "Rc2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen"